export const GUIDE_TEXT: string = "<guide label=\"Step 1\" title=\"Get your link\">\nGoal: One class is live, Stripe is connected, and the link is in a family's hands.\n\nThree things and you're live: build a class, connect Stripe, share the link.\n\n## Sign up {#sign-up}\n\n**Goal:** your own registration page at `enrops.com/your-business`.\n\n**Steps**\n1. Go to enrops.com/signup.\n2. Tap **Continue with Google**, or type your email and tap **Email me a sign-in link**.\n3. Type your business name and tap **Create my free page →**.\n4. You'll see \"Your registration page is ready.\" with your page address. Tap **Build your first program →**.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- No password to remember. Every time you come back, sign in the same way you did today: Google, or an emailed link.\n- Your page address comes from your business name. You can change it later in **Settings → Your page address**. Do that before you share any links, because old links stop working when it changes.\n- We set you up with starter waivers and a starter cancellation policy so your page isn't missing anything. Read them before you share your link (see **Make it yours**).\n\n**If it goes wrong**\n- No email arrived: check spam, then ask for a new link. Links expire, so use the newest one.\n- School and work email addresses sometimes block sign-in links. A personal Gmail is the most reliable.\n\n## Build your first class {#first-program}\n\n**Goal:** one class with a name, a place, dates and a price.\n\n**What to have ready:** class name, where it happens, day and time, first class date, price per child, how many kids you can take. A short description and a photo help families decide, but you can add them later.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Programs → Scheduled programs → + New program.** Your very first time, you go straight there from signup.\n2. The first time, you get three quick questions:\n   - **Where do your classes happen?** At our own space / We go out to schools or other sites / A bit of both.\n   - **How do your classes usually run?** A weekly series / One-off workshops / A bit of both.\n   - **What ages do you teach?** Leave it blank if it varies.\n\n   Then tap **Next: build my first class →**. (**Not now** skips them, and they come back next time.)\n3. Fill in **Program name**, **Price** and **Spots**. Add a **Description** and **Photo** if you have them.\n4. Pick the **Location** (or **Which site?**). Use **+ Add a location** (or **+ Add a site**) if it's new. Choose its **District**, or **No district (studio, library, private site)**. If it's at a school, tick **This is at a school or another organization's site** so you can send them rosters. Tap **Save location**.\n5. Choose **What kind of thing is this?**\n   - **Weekly series:** day of the week, start and end time, **First class date**, **# of classes**.\n   - **One-off workshop:** the date.\n   - **Camp:** days it runs, half or full day, first and last day, times.\n6. Add **Who it's for** (grades or ages) if you like.\n7. Tap **Create program & get link**. If Stripe isn't connected yet, the button says **Save draft & connect Stripe →**. It saves your class first, so nothing you typed is lost.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- Under the price you'll see \"Families pay $X\". That's the number to put on your flyer, because it's what families actually pay.\n- Not sure of your price? Publish your best number. You can change it before families register, and anyone who already registered keeps the price they paid.\n- Write the description outcome first: what kids walk away with.\n- A weekly class needs a **First class date** before it can go live. You can save a draft without one.\n- If the first class date falls on a different weekday than the day you picked, the dates follow the date. Check the dates preview.\n\n**If it goes wrong**\n- You see \"This location has no district yet, so these class dates won't skip no-school days.\" Your dates will include school holidays until you fix it. See **Make your dates skip no-school days**.\n\n## Make your dates skip no-school days {#school-calendar}\n\n**Goal:** class dates skip holidays, breaks and teacher work days automatically.\n\n**When you need it:** any class at a school, or any class whose families follow a school calendar. Do it before you share your link, because families see the dates.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Programs → Locations.** Tap **Open** on the site, choose its **District**, and tap **Save changes**. Pick **No district (library, church, private site)** only if it truly doesn't follow a school calendar.\n2. **Programs → School calendar.** Find the district and tap **Add calendar**.\n3. Under **Pull dates…**, paste a link to the district calendar, upload the PDF, or paste the text, then tap **Extract**.\n4. Check **First day of school**, **Last day of school**, **No-school days** and **Early-release days**. Fix anything that's off and tap **Save calendar**.\n5. When asked whether you teach on early-release days, choose **Yes, I teach on early-release days** (and the time) or **No, we skip those days**.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- The district is the piece people miss. Everything looks saved and the dates are simply wrong. Every school site needs one.\n- One district calendar covers every school in that district. You only upload it once per school year.\n- The early-release answer can be changed later with the **Class times** button on that calendar's row.\n- A single day off (a field trip, a snow day): **Programs → Scheduled programs**, open the class, **Mark a no-school day**.\n\n**If it goes wrong**\n- The banner says \"No calendar saved for (district)\": that district's dates are weekly only, with no holidays taken out. Tap the link in the banner to add the calendar.\n- An early-release day shows as no class: open the calendar's **Class times** and choose **Yes, I teach on early-release days**.\n\n## Connect Stripe so families can pay you {#connect-stripe}\n\n**Goal:** families pay you by card or bank transfer, and the money goes into your own account.\n\n**What to have ready:** your business's legal name, EIN (or your SSN if you're a sole owner), business address, date of birth, a photo ID, and your bank account and routing number. This is Stripe's standard check for anyone taking card payments.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Money → Payments.**\n2. Already use Stripe? Tap **Connect my Stripe account** and pick the account you already have. New to Stripe? Tap **I don't use Stripe yet**.\n3. Finish Stripe's form. When you come back, the page shows **Stripe connected · Charges on · Payouts on**.\n4. Stopped partway? Come back to **Money → Payments** and tap **Continue setup**. Finished but the page hasn't caught up? Tap **Already finished? Check status**.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- The screen says connecting takes about a minute if you already use Stripe, and 5 to 10 minutes if not.\n- enrops never sees your bank or tax details. They go straight into Stripe's secure form.\n- Payment goes into your Stripe account, then Stripe pays it to your bank on its own schedule. On Stripe's standard US schedule a payment arrives about 2 business days later. Your very first payout can take longer while Stripe reviews a new account.\n- Pick the right button first time. **I don't use Stripe yet** creates a new Stripe account straight away, and if you already had one you'll need **Disconnect Stripe** to switch.\n\n**If it goes wrong**\n- Stripe asks for a code from its phone app or a passkey you don't have: look for another way to verify on that Stripe screen (such as a text message). If there isn't one, stop there and email hello@enrops.com with what the screen says.\n- Stripe says your name or address doesn't match government records: fix it on Stripe's account page and upload the document it asks for.\n- \"This organization already has a Stripe account connected\": open **Payment settings** on **Money → Payments** and disconnect the current one first.\n\n## Publish it and share your link {#share-link}\n\n**Goal:** families can find your class and register.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Programs → Scheduled programs.** A draft shows **Publish →**. Tap it and confirm.\n2. Tap **Share** on the class (or **Share registration page** at the top for all your classes).\n3. **Copy** the link, or tap **QR code → Download PNG** for your flyer.\n4. Tap **Preview the registration page ↗** and walk through it on your phone, the way a parent would.\n5. Have your own website? On **Programs**, tap **Add to your website** and **Copy code**, then paste it into your site.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- Check it on your phone too, not just a computer.\n- At checkout families see your price plus the enrops service fee on its own line, so nobody is surprised.\n- Where to send it: the principal or front office, your school newsletter contact, and the families you already know.\n- If families can't see a class, the share panel says **Not open to families** and gives no link. That happens when the class starts more than a year from now, or, if you open one term at a time, when its term isn't open yet. Camps are the exception: their link works as soon as you publish. See **When families see your classes**.\n\n**If it goes wrong**\n- The share button says **Connect Stripe to share your link →**: families can't pay until Stripe is connected.\n- \"Not live yet. Publish this program first\": tap **Publish →** on the class.\n\n## Where registrations show up {#see-registrations}\n\n- **Programs → Scheduled programs** shows enrolled / spots for each class.\n- Once a class has started, it also shows whether families can still sign up: **In progress · 4 of 8 sessions left** (still taking sign-ups, at a price for the sessions left), **Sign-ups closed · class started** (you've turned off **Settings → Late sign-ups**), or **Sign-ups closed · class finished**.\n- **Programs → Class rosters** lists every child. Anyone who registers through enrops shows up automatically.\n- \"(+N unfinished registrations, not counted)\" means a family started but didn't pay. They aren't on your roster yet.\n- Payments: **Money → Payments** shows what came in. Your actual bank deposits are in your Stripe dashboard (**Stripe Dashboard ↗**).\n</guide>\n\n<guide label=\"Step 2\" title=\"Make it yours\">\nGoal: Families see your logo, read your words, and reply to you.\n\nWe set you up with sensible starting points. This is where you make them yours. Each one takes a few minutes.\n\n## Save your registration questions {#registration-questions}\n\n**Goal:** your form asks exactly what you need to know, including how each child goes home.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Settings → Registration questions → Manage →**.\n2. Under **Optional standard questions**, check the pickup and dismissal questions. If you told us your classes are at schools or other sites, they were added when you built your first class.\n3. Under **Ways a family can say their child leaves**, tick every option you actually allow: released to a parent or authorized adult, walks or bikes home, takes the bus, goes to aftercare, something else.\n4. Tap **Save standard questions**.\n5. To ask something of your own, tap **+ Add question** under **Your own questions**. Pick the **Answer type**, choose whether to ask it on every program or one class, and tap **Add question**.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- Changes here only reach your form when you tap **Save standard questions**. The page warns you if something is unsaved.\n- **Takes the bus** and **Something else** start switched off. If any of your kids ride a bus, tick **Takes the bus**, or families can't tell you.\n- Your form always asks for the child's name, grade and birth date, allergies and medical notes, an emergency contact, the parent's name, email and phone, and a mailing address. You don't need to add those.\n- Pick the answer type carefully. A question that needs words should be **Short text** or **Long text**, not a checkbox.\n\n## Read your waivers and cancellation policy {#waivers}\n\n**Goal:** families agree to wording you're comfortable with.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Settings → Waivers & policies → Manage →**.\n2. Under **Waivers families sign**, open each one with **Edit**. You start with three: participation and liability, medical and emergency care (both required), and a photo and media release (families can decline).\n3. Under **Policies you publish**, open the **Cancellation & Refund Policy**. Edit it, or leave it as is.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- We wrote the starter cancellation policy so your page wasn't missing one. These are our words, not yours, and they make promises about refunds. Out of the box it says: a full refund before the first session, a refund for sessions not yet attended once a class has started, no refund after it ends, and a full refund if you cancel. Change anything that isn't how you run it.\n- Leave **{{org}}** where it is in a waiver. Families see your business name there.\n- The starter wording is a helpful beginning, not legal advice. Have a lawyer read anything that really matters to your business.\n\n## Add your logo and page wording {#branding}\n\n**Goal:** your page and your emails look like your business.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Settings → Branding → Manage →**.\n2. **Logo:** tap **Upload logo** (SVG, PNG, JPG or WebP, under 2 MB).\n3. **Colors:** after you upload, we suggest colors \"Found in your logo\". Tap **Use these** if you like them.\n4. **Banner** (optional): a wide photo across the top of your registration page, about 3 times wider than it is tall.\n5. **Registration page wording:** a **Headline** and a **Line underneath**. Leave them blank to use the default.\n6. **Confirmation page wording:** what families see after they pay. You can add a button, like \"Visit our shop\", with a link.\n7. Tap **Save**. Nothing you upload is kept until you save.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- Your logo appears on your registration pages and in your emails.\n- Use the confirmation page to say what happens next: when the first class is, what to bring, and how to reach you.\n\n## Make sure family replies reach you {#email-sender}\n\n**Goal:** when a family hits reply, it lands in the inbox you actually read.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Settings → Email sender → Manage →**.\n2. Check **Sender name**. It defaults to your business name.\n3. Set **Reply-to email** to the inbox you check.\n4. Add your **Mailing address**. The law requires it on marketing emails.\n5. Set **Where should we send your alerts?** if you want enrops alerts somewhere other than your sign-in email.\n6. Tap **Save**, then **Send test** to see an email the way families see it.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- If you leave reply-to blank, replies go to the email you signed up with. The page tells you which one it's using.\n- Your emails are sent from an enrops address named after your page address, so you never have to touch domain settings. Families still see your name.\n\n## Add a teammate {#team}\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Team → Invite teammate**.\n2. Type their email and choose a role, then tap **Send invite**:\n   - **Admin:** everything, including money and settings.\n   - **Staff:** run programs, rosters and emails, but no money or settings.\n   - **Viewer:** read-only, and can't see money.\n3. They get a sign-in link by email.\n\n## Things you can't change yourself yet {#not-yet-settings}\n\n- **Time zone:** set from your browser when you signed up. To change it, email hello@enrops.com.\n- **Business name:** email hello@enrops.com.\n</guide>\n\n<guide label=\"Step 3\" title=\"Fill your classes\">\nGoal: Families who already know you hear about the class.\n\n## Bring in the families you already know {#import-families}\n\n**Goal:** your existing family list lives in enrops, so you can email them about classes.\n\n**What to have ready:** a spreadsheet (.csv, .xlsx or .xls), or a PDF or Word document. Email is the only column you must have. Parent name, phone, child's name, school and birthdate all help.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Comms → Contacts → Upload contacts →**.\n2. **Choose your file**, then **Read file →**.\n3. Match your columns to ours. Only **Email** is required.\n4. Optional: tag everyone in this upload, for example \"Lincoln families 2025\".\n5. Choose **New families** (they get your welcome email if it's on) or **My existing families** (no welcome, for people who already know you).\n6. Tick **I have permission to email these contacts.** and tap **Add N contacts**.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- A PDF or Word list works too. We read it for you, then you check the columns before anything is saved.\n- Only upload families who agreed to hear from you. The upload asks you to confirm that.\n\n## Email the families in a class {#message-families}\n\n**Goal:** send one email to everyone in one or more classes.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Programs → Class rosters.**\n2. Tick the classes, then tap **Message families (N classes)**.\n3. Optional: include families on the waiting list, or families who left or were refunded.\n4. Write a **Subject** and your message. Use **Send a test to** to check it first, or tick **Email me a copy**.\n5. Tap **Send to N families**. Sent emails are listed on the **Sent** tab.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- The count is families, not children. Two siblings in one class get one email.\n- Send yourself a test first. It's the fastest way to catch a typo or a broken link.\n\n## Sibling discounts and promo codes {#discounts}\n\n**Steps (sibling discount)**\n1. **Money → Discounts.**\n2. Under the sibling discount, type a percent, for example 10. That's taken off each additional child in the same order. Leave it blank to turn it off.\n3. Tap **Save**.\n\n**Steps (promo code)**\n1. **Money → Discounts → + New code.**\n2. Type the **Code**, choose **% off** or **$ off**, and set **Starts** and **Ends** dates.\n3. Optional: limit **Total uses**, uses **Per family**, a minimum order (**Min. cart**), or which programs it **Applies to**.\n4. Tap **Create code**.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- A family with two children is deciding whether to sign up twice. A small automatic discount usually costs you less than losing that second registration.\n- Give each code a reason and an end date. Open-ended codes get passed around and quietly become your new price.\n- A 100% code means families pay nothing. Use it for a scholarship or a make-up class.\n- Codes apply on top of sibling savings.\n\n## Families who started but didn't finish {#unfinished-registrations}\n\n- A roster shows \"(+N unfinished registrations, not counted)\" when a family started registering but didn't pay. They aren't enrolled yet and haven't paid.\n- Automatic follow-up emails to these families aren't on the free plan. Email hello@enrops.com if you need it.\n</guide>\n\n<guide label=\"Step 4\" title=\"Run the term\">\nGoal: Families get a welcome and your school partner has the roster.\n\nTwo weeks out, make sure families know what's coming and your school knows who's coming.\n\n## Turn on your automatic emails {#automations}\n\n**Goal:** families get the right email at the right time without you sending it.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Comms → Automations.**\n2. Read each email and tap **Turn on** for the ones you want.\n\n**What each one does**\n- **Thank-you:** sent when a registration is paid. Always on once Stripe is connected.\n- **Welcome (after-school or camp):** sent before the first class. Off until you turn it on.\n- **No-school day heads-up:** reminds families when class doesn't meet. Off until you turn it on.\n- **New class photos:** tells families when photos are posted. On.\n- **Payment coming up:** reminds families on a payment plan before a payment. On.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- The welcome email is off until you turn it on.\n- Read each email before you turn it on. You're the one families will reply to.\n- If your families register on your own website instead of enrops, these emails don't send.\n\n## Your rosters {#rosters}\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Programs → Class rosters.** Use **Search school or class** to find one.\n2. **View / print →** opens a class. From there you can **Download CSV**, **Print**, or **Email roster to partner**.\n3. To add a child yourself: **Add / upload → Add one by hand**. Only the first name is required. Tap **Add to roster**.\n4. To upload a list: **Add / upload → Upload a file** (.csv or .xlsx). Check the rows, then **Import N students**.\n5. To fix a child's details: expand the class and tap **View / Edit →**.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- When you add a child by hand, the photo release box starts ticked. Untick it if the family hasn't agreed, and the child shows as pending until they do.\n- **Remove** only appears for families who haven't paid, and it can't be undone. For a family who paid, use **Refund / remove** (see **Money moments**).\n\n## Send the roster to your school partner {#roster-to-partner}\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Programs → Class rosters → View / print →** on the class.\n2. Tap **Email roster to partner**.\n3. If the site isn't linked to a school partner yet, you're asked to pick one. If none are listed, go to **Programs → Locations**, open the site, and tap **Add as a school partner**.\n4. Tick the contacts who should get it, or type other emails separated by commas. To add the school's contacts: **Programs → Locations**, **Open** the school, then **Contacts → + Add contact**.\n5. Tap **Send roster**. The roster is attached as a PDF, and the subject is filled in from the class details.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- Send it before class one, and again if anyone joins late.\n\n## Invite families to the parent portal {#invite-families}\n\n**Goal:** families can sign in, see class details, and update their own pickup information.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Programs → Class rosters → Invite families →** on the class.\n2. Check the preview. It shows how many families will get it and what the email says.\n3. Tap **Send N invites**.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- Families who already signed in, or have no email on file, are skipped, so it's safe to send again.\n- Families don't need an invite. They can always go to your page, tap sign in, and get a sign-in link by email.\n- In the portal, families sign your required waivers before they see class details.\n\n## Instructors {#instructors}\n\nInstructor tools (onboarding, schedule, subs, attendance and pay) are part of the founding and enterprise plans. If **Instructors** isn't in your menu, they aren't on your plan yet. Email hello@enrops.com if you'd like to use them.\n\nWhen you do have them:\n- **Instructors → Instructor Roster → + Add instructor**, then **Send onboarding invite**.\n- Instructors sign in at your page address plus `/instructor`.\n- Putting an instructor on a class doesn't email them. Send the offer when you're ready.\n- Instructors take attendance and record who picked each child up in their portal. You read it in **Programs → Class Reports**.\n</guide>\n\n<guide label=\"Step 5\" title=\"Money moments\">\nGoal: You know where your money is, and you can refund or credit a family in a minute.\n\n## How you get paid {#how-you-get-paid}\n\n- A family pays. The money goes into your own Stripe account.\n- Stripe pays it out to your bank. On Stripe's standard US schedule that's about 2 business days after the payment. Bank-transfer payments take 1 to 3 business days to clear first. Your first payout can take longer while Stripe reviews a new account.\n- **Money → Payments** shows the class fees that came in, refunds, and what's expected soon.\n- Your actual bank deposits are in your Stripe dashboard. Tap **Open Stripe →** or **Stripe Dashboard ↗**.\n\n## What families pay, and what enrops takes {#fees}\n\n- Families pay your price plus the enrops service fee. They see it on its own line before they pay.\n- Stripe takes its standard processing fee before the money reaches your bank. That's Stripe's charge, the same as with any card payment tool.\n- The price screen shows exactly what families pay: \"Families pay $X\". Use that number anywhere you advertise.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- Families see the fee before they pay, on purpose. Costs that appear at the last step are the number one reason people abandon an online order (40%, according to the Baymard Institute). Shown up front, the same cost doesn't do that.\n- Call it the \"enrops service fee\", the same words families see at checkout.\n\n## Refund a family {#refund}\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Programs → Class rosters.** Expand the class.\n2. Tap **Refund / remove** on the family's row.\n3. Choose **What they get**: **Refund to their card**, or **Give enrops credit instead**.\n4. For a card refund, choose **Their spot**: **Refund only — keep their spot**, or **Refund and withdraw — free their spot**. For a credit there's no spot choice, because a credit always frees their spot. Instead choose who ended it: **We cancelled the class** or **The family cancelled**.\n5. Leave **Full refund**, or type a smaller amount for a partial refund.\n6. Add a **Reason**. It's an internal note and isn't sent to the family.\n7. Tap **Refund $X** (or **Give $X credit**).\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- The family gets an email receipt for a card refund. A credit or a withdrawal without a refund sends no email, so tell them yourself.\n- A refund takes 5 to 10 business days to show on the family's card.\n- Before the class starts, the enrops service fee is refunded in full. After it starts, only the share for sessions not yet held comes back. Stripe's processing cost isn't returned when a payment is refunded. That stays with your business, which is standard for card payments.\n- Credit is applied automatically the next time that family registers with the same email address. Credit can't be used on a payment plan.\n- Money → Payments → **Refunds** lists every refund you've made.\n\n## Cancel a whole class {#cancel-class}\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Programs → Scheduled programs.** Expand the class and tap **Cancel class**.\n2. Confirm with **Cancel the class**.\n3. Cancelling doesn't refund anyone or send any emails. Go to **Programs → Class rosters**, open the class, and refund each family.\n4. Tell families. Use **Message families** and tick **Also include families who have left or been refunded**, so the ones you just refunded get it too.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- A rule of thumb: when you cancel, refund the family. When the family cancels, offer credit.\n- Changed your mind? **Reopen as draft** brings the class back.\n\n## Stop selling a class {#stop-selling}\n\n- A published class keeps taking registrations after it has started. It comes off your page after its last session (see **When families see your classes**). There's no close date you can set yet.\n- To stop sign-ups for every class once it has started, turn off **Settings → Late sign-ups**.\n- To stop it, open the class in **Programs → Scheduled programs** and tap **Unpublish**. It goes back to draft, and families already registered stay registered.\n</guide>\n\n<guide label=\"Step 6\" title=\"Next term\">\nGoal: Next term's classes are copied, dated and open, and this term's families hear first.\n\n## Copy your classes to the next term {#copy-to-term}\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Programs → Scheduled programs.** Make sure the term picker shows the term you're copying from.\n2. Tap **Copy classes to another term**. Tick the classes, choose the term the new dates fall in (see **What the term codes mean**), and copy. Camps aren't included here, so copy each camp on its own. (For one class or camp: expand it, and under **Copy to another term** pick the season and year, then tap **Copy to (term) →**.)\n3. Switch the term picker to the new term to find the copies. They're drafts.\n4. Expand each copy and set its **First class date**. A copy can't be published until it has one.\n5. Check the price and times, then **Publish →**.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- Copies come over without dates on purpose, so you can't publish last term's dates by accident.\n- Before you publish, check the school calendar for the new term is saved (see **Make your dates skip no-school days**).\n\n## When families see your classes {#open-term}\n\n- Most providers have nothing to switch. Your page shows weekly classes up to a year ahead, so a class for January or next summer is on sale as soon as you publish it, even while this term's classes are still running.\n- Each weekly class stays on your page until its last session, then comes off on its own. Families already enrolled aren't affected. To stop sign-ups sooner, **Unpublish** it.\n- A family who joins after a class has started pays only for the sessions left, and the card says how many are left. Don't want late sign-ups at all? Turn off **Settings → Late sign-ups**, and every class stops taking sign-ups once its first session has happened.\n- Camps stay on your page until their last day, whatever the season.\n- If Programs shows **Open (term) for registration →**, your account opens one term at a time instead. Tapping it switches your page to that term's weekly classes, and the old term's stop showing.\n\n**Ennie's advice**\n- When next term's classes are published, tell this term's families first with **Message families**.\n\n## What the term codes mean {#term-codes}\n\n- A term code is a season plus a two-digit year: **FA** fall, **WI** winter, **SP** spring, **SU** summer. **WI27** is winter 2027.\n- Winter is December to February, spring March to May, summer June to August, fall September to November. A class starting in December is in the next year's winter.\n</guide>\n\n<guide label=\"Questions\" title=\"Questions providers ask\">\nEach answer is short and points to the guide with the full steps. \"Not yet\" means it can't be done today.\n\n## Getting started\n\n### How do I sign in? {#faq-sign-in}\nGo to enrops.com/login and use Google, or tap **Email me a sign-in link**. There's no password. See **Sign up**.\n\n### Do I need a curriculum document to make a class? {#faq-curriculum}\nNo. Type a name, a short description and a price. See **Build your first class**.\n\n### Can I change things after my class is live? {#faq-edit-live}\nYes. The name, price, times and dates can all be edited after you publish. Families who already registered keep the price they paid.\n\n### Can I put registration on my own website? {#faq-embed}\nYes. On **Programs**, tap **Add to your website** and **Copy code**. Or link to your page, or print the QR code. See **Publish it and share your link**.\n\n### Can families see only their own school's classes? {#faq-school-picker}\nYes. If your classes are at more than one location, families pick their school first, and only then see its classes and prices.\n\n## Payments and fees\n\n### Where does the money go, and when do I get it? {#faq-payouts}\nInto your own Stripe account. Then Stripe pays your bank, about 2 business days after each payment on its standard US schedule. Your first payout can take longer. See **How you get paid**.\n\n### What does enrops cost me? {#faq-cost}\nenrops is free for businesses. Families pay a small enrops service fee with each registration, shown on its own line before they pay. The price screen shows exactly what families pay. Stripe's standard processing fee also applies, as with any card payment tool. See **What families pay**.\n\n### Can I cover the fee myself instead of families? {#faq-cover-fee}\nYes. **Money → Payments → Who pays the enrops service fee?** Switch it from **Pass-through** to **Absorbed**. Families then pay only your price, and the fee comes out of your payout instead. This setting shows once Stripe is connected.\n\n### Why are two prices different when I didn't set a discount? {#faq-two-prices}\nIt's usually the sibling discount. Check **Money → Discounts**. Leave the sibling box blank to turn it off.\n\n### Does the fee apply to merchandise? {#faq-merch}\nMerchandise doesn't run through enrops checkout yet. Keep selling it the way you do today.\n\n### I stopped partway through Stripe. How do I get back in? {#faq-stripe-resume}\n**Money → Payments → Continue setup**. It picks up where you left off. See **Connect Stripe**.\n\n### Stripe wants a code or passkey I don't have. {#faq-stripe-passkey}\nLook for another way to verify on that Stripe screen, such as a text message. If there isn't one, stop and email hello@enrops.com with what it says.\n\n### Can I use the Stripe account I already have? {#faq-stripe-existing}\nYes. Tap **Connect my Stripe account**, not **I don't use Stripe yet**.\n\n## Dates and terms\n\n### My class dates include a school holiday. {#faq-holiday}\nThe location probably has no district, or the district has no calendar saved. See **Make your dates skip no-school days**.\n\n### An early-release day was imported as no class. How do I add it back? {#faq-early-release}\n**Programs → School calendar**, tap **Class times** on that calendar, and choose **Yes, I teach on early-release days**.\n\n### How do I cancel just one session? {#faq-one-session}\nMark it as a no-school day: open the class and tap **Mark a no-school day**. Choose **Just this school**, or every class in that district skips the date too. The schedule runs a week longer and families see the new dates.\n\n### What does FA26 or WI27 mean? {#faq-term-codes}\nSeason plus year: FA fall, WI winter, SP spring, SU summer. WI27 is winter 2027. Winter is December to February, so a class starting in December or January is in winter. A class goes in the season of its first class.\n\n### How do I copy my classes to next term? {#faq-copy-term}\n**Copy classes to another term** on Programs. Copies are drafts and need a first class date before you publish. See **Copy your classes to the next term**.\n\n### Can I run a year-long class? {#faq-year-long}\nNot yet as its own option. Email hello@enrops.com.\n\n## Registration form and waivers\n\n### How do I add my own question to the form? {#faq-custom-question}\n**Settings → Registration questions → + Add question**. Pick **Short text** if you want words back, not a checkbox. See **Save your registration questions**.\n\n### Where do I change what families see after they pay? {#faq-confirmation-page}\n**Settings → Branding → Confirmation page wording**. You can add a button and a link there.\n\n### Can the photo release be required? {#faq-photo-release}\nFamilies can decline the photo release. A child without one on file shows as pending when you add them by hand.\n\n### Who wrote my cancellation policy? {#faq-policy}\nWe did, so your page wasn't missing one. Read it and make it yours. See **Read your waivers and cancellation policy**.\n\n## Families\n\n### A parent's email bounced. How do I fix it? {#faq-fix-email}\n**Comms → Contacts**, find the family, and tap **Edit**.\n\n### How do parents get into the parent portal? {#faq-parent-portal}\nThey go to your page, tap sign in, and get a link by email. To nudge them, use **Invite families →** on the class roster. See **Invite families to the parent portal**.\n\n### Can a second parent get their own login? {#faq-second-parent}\nNot yet. Only the parent who registered can sign in. The second parent does get the messages you send from **Message families**.\n\n### Can I add or remove a family contact by hand? {#faq-contact-add-remove}\nNot yet from the Contacts screen. You can add a child to a roster by hand (see **Your rosters**).\n\n### How do I see the waitlist? {#faq-waitlist}\nOpen the class with **View / print →**. The **Waitlist** section lists families in order. When a place opens, the next family in line is emailed and has 24 hours to take it. If they don't, it goes to the next family.\n\n### Can I export my families or payments? {#faq-export}\nYou can download a class roster as a CSV from **View / print →**. Payments are in your Stripe dashboard. For anything else, email hello@enrops.com.\n\n## Emails\n\n### Did my email actually go out? {#faq-sent}\nEmails sent from **Message families** are listed on its **Sent** tab.\n\n### Can I test an email before sending it? {#faq-test-email}\nYes. Use **Send a test to** or **Email me a copy** in Message families, and **Send test** under **Settings → Email sender**.\n\n### Why did a parent's reply go somewhere else? {#faq-reply-to}\nCheck **Settings → Email sender → Reply-to email**. If it's blank, replies go to the email you signed up with.\n\n### Can I add a photo to an email to families? {#faq-email-photo}\nNot yet.\n\n### Can I text families or instructors? {#faq-sms}\nNot yet.\n\n### Why does \"Message families\" say fewer families than kids? {#faq-family-count}\nIt counts families, not children. Siblings share one email.\n\n## Rosters and refunds\n\n### What does \"unfinished registration\" mean? {#faq-unfinished}\nA family started registering and didn't pay. They aren't on your roster yet.\n\n### How do I refund a family? {#faq-refund}\n**Programs → Class rosters**, expand the class, tap **Refund / remove**. See **Refund a family**.\n\n### Does a class stop selling when it starts? {#faq-close}\nNot when it starts. It comes off your page after its last session (see **When families see your classes**). To stop sign-ups once every class has started, turn off **Settings → Late sign-ups**. To stop one class sooner, **Unpublish** it. See **Stop selling a class**.\n\n### What does a family pay if they join late? {#faq-late-join}\nOnly for the sessions left: the price × sessions left ÷ total sessions. A family joining an 8-session $275 class with 4 sessions left pays $137.50. Their card and checkout say \"Started Nov 2 · 4 of 8 sessions left\". Sibling discounts and promo codes still apply.\n\n### Why does my page say \"No open programs yet\"? {#faq-no-programs}\nEvery published class has either finished, or started while **Settings → Late sign-ups** is off. Publish your next classes, or turn Late sign-ups back on.\n\n### How do I send the roster to the school? {#faq-roster-partner}\n**View / print → Email roster to partner**. See **Send the roster to your school partner**.\n\n## Instructors (founding and enterprise plans)\n\n### How do I add a teacher? {#faq-add-instructor}\n**Instructors → Instructor Roster → + Add instructor**, then **Send onboarding invite**.\n\n### A teacher with a school email keeps getting signed out. {#faq-school-email}\nSchool and work email systems sometimes block sign-in links. A personal Gmail is the most reliable.\n\n### Can I turn off the sub coordination email? {#faq-sub-email}\nNot yet.\n\n## Getting help\n\n### Who do I ask? {#faq-help}\nTap Ennie in the bottom-right corner to ask a question. Ennie answers from these guides and links the part it used. If the guides don't cover it, tap **Send to the enrops team** and the chat comes to us. You can also tap **Talk to a person** in the chat, tap **Share feedback** in the menu, or email hello@enrops.com. A real person on the enrops team answers.\n</guide>";

